# Planning & Goals Rules
# Loaded when planning, goal setting, or strategic coordination tasks are required
# Auto-generated by Dynamic Cursor Rules System
# Integrates Phase 3 Standards: Goal Tree, KPI Metrics, Task Dependency Map, Project Plans, System Hierarchy

## PLANNING & GOALS STANDARDS (PHASE 3)

### Core Principle: Strategic Alignment & Measurable Progress
**These rules ensure all work traces to the North Star and progress is measurable and trackable.**

---

## 🎯 **GOAL TREE STANDARDS**

### Three-Level Hierarchy
**Level 1: North Star** (The Vision)
- Single ultimate goal
- Inspiring and clear
- Time-bound
- Achievable but ambitious

**Level 2: Objectives** (Strategic Pillars)
- 4-10 major objectives
- Each serves the North Star
- Specific and focused
- Owner-assigned
- Time-bound

**Level 3: Key Results** (Measurable Outcomes)
- 2-5 KRs per objective
- Quantitative and measurable
- Specific targets
- Progress trackable
- Success verifiable

### Goal Tree Requirements
- **Always trace to North Star** - Every task must connect to ≥1 objective
- **Measurable Key Results** - All KRs must be quantifiable
- **Owner Assignment** - Every objective has clear owner
- **Time-bound** - All objectives have target dates
- **Status Tracking** - Track completion percentage for all objectives
- **Regular Review** - Update goal tree regularly (weekly/monthly)

### Goal Alignment Validation
**Before starting ANY task:**
- Can you trace it to North Star? (goals/GOAL_TREE.yaml)
- Does it serve ≥1 objective?
- Does it advance ≥1 key result?
- If NO to any → Don't do it (cosmetic work, drift)

### Goal Tree Structure Requirements
- **Metadata:** Complete frontmatter with id, version, north_star, total_objectives, total_key_results
- **North Star:** Single ultimate goal statement
- **Objectives:** Array of objectives with id, name, description, owner, target_date, priority
- **Key Results:** Array of KRs with id, metric, baseline, target, current, unit, measurement_method
- **Status Tracking:** completion_percentage, status (planned/in_progress/blocked/complete)

---

## 📊 **KPI METRICS STANDARDS**

### KPI Requirements
- **Quantitative Metrics** - All KPIs must be measurable
- **Baseline Establishment** - Know starting point
- **Target Setting** - Define success criteria
- **Trend Tracking** - Track over time
- **Threshold Definition** - Critical/warning/excellent thresholds
- **Regular Collection** - Daily/weekly/monthly collection

### KPI Structure Requirements
- **Metadata:** Complete frontmatter with id, version, collection_frequency, total_kpis, active_kpis
- **KPI Definition:** id, name, description, category, metric_type, unit
- **Measurement:** baseline, target, current, thresholds, direction (higher_is_better/lower_is_better)
- **Collection:** collection_method, collection_frequency, data_source, owner
- **Tracking:** status, trend, last_measured, history array
- **Connection:** related_goal (KR link)

### KPI Selection Criteria
- **Measurable** - Can we collect data?
- **Meaningful** - Does it matter?
- **Actionable** - Can we improve it?
- **Aligned** - Links to Key Results
- **Balanced** - Leading and lagging indicators

### KPI Usage Rules
- **Track regularly** - Don't let metrics go stale
- **Review trends** - Look for patterns
- **Act on signals** - Respond to threshold breaches
- **Report progress** - Include in status reports
- **Update targets** - Adjust based on progress

---

## 📋 **TASK DEPENDENCY MAP STANDARDS**

### DAG Structure Requirements
- **Directed Acyclic Graph** - Tasks have dependencies, no cycles
- **Complete Dependencies** - All dependencies documented
- **Priority Calculation** - Systematic priority formula
- **Critical Path** - Identify longest path
- **Status Tracking** - Track completion status

### Task Structure Requirements
- **Metadata:** Complete frontmatter with id, version, total_tasks, completed_tasks, critical_path_length
- **Task Definition:** id, name, description
- **Metrics:** priority (0.0-1.0), confidence (0.0-1.0), complexity (0.0-1.0), estimated_hours
- **Dependencies:** dependencies (must complete), blocks (blocks these), related_tasks (related but not dependent)
- **Status:** status (pending/in_progress/complete/blocked/cancelled), completion (0-100%), started, completed
- **Assignment:** assigned_to, reviewer
- **Context:** systems_involved, goal_alignment (KR link), risk_level
- **Outcomes:** deliverables, success_criteria, validation_method

### Priority Calculation Formula
```
Priority = (0.40 × goal_impact) + (0.25 × urgency) + (0.20 × confidence) + (0.10 × dependency_impact) - (0.05 × risk)
```

**Always choose highest priority task that meets confidence threshold (≥0.70)**

### Task Dependency Rules
- **Never work on blocked tasks** - Wait for dependencies
- **Track completion** - Update status regularly
- **Calculate critical path** - Focus on bottleneck tasks
- **Identify parallel work** - Work on independent tasks simultaneously
- **Update dependencies** - Keep dependency map current

---

## 📅 **PROJECT PLAN STANDARDS**

### Project Plan Structure Requirements
- **Metadata:** Complete frontmatter with id, version, project_name, start_date, target_date, status
- **Project Overview:** name, description, objectives, success_criteria
- **Timeline:** phases, milestones, deadlines
- **Resources:** team, budget, tools
- **Risks:** risk_register, mitigation_plans
- **Status:** current_status, progress_percentage, blockers

### Project Planning Rules
- **Define phases** - Break project into phases
- **Set milestones** - Track major achievements
- **Allocate resources** - Assign team and budget
- **Identify risks** - Document potential issues
- **Track progress** - Regular status updates
- **Adjust timeline** - Update based on reality

---

## 🏗️ **SYSTEM HIERARCHY STANDARDS**

### Hierarchy Structure Requirements
- **Metadata:** Complete frontmatter with id, version, hierarchy_type, total_systems
- **Hierarchy Levels:** Tier 0 (core), Tier 1 (enhanced), Tier 2 (supporting), Tier 3 (auxiliary)
- **System Relationships:** parent-child, dependencies, interactions
- **Organization:** logical grouping, clear categorization

### System Hierarchy Rules
- **Organize by tier** - Core → Enhanced → Supporting → Auxiliary
- **Document relationships** - Parent-child, dependencies
- **Maintain consistency** - Use consistent categorization
- **Update regularly** - Keep hierarchy current
- **Cross-reference** - Link to system maps and indexes

---

## 🔗 **INTEGRATION REQUIREMENTS**

### Cross-Standard Integration
- **Goal Tree → KPI Metrics:** All KRs link to KPIs
- **Goal Tree → Task Dependency Map:** All tasks link to KRs
- **Task Dependency Map → Project Plans:** Tasks organized into project phases
- **All → System Hierarchy:** Systems organized hierarchically

### MCP Tool Integration
- **Use `mcp_lucid-mcp_create_goal_timeline_node`** for creating goals
- **Use `mcp_lucid-mcp_update_goal_progress`** for tracking progress
- **Use `mcp_lucid-mcp_query_goal_timeline`** for querying goals
- **Use `mcp_lucid-mcp_create_plan`** for creating execution plans

---

## ✅ **QUALITY REQUIREMENTS**

### Planning Quality Standards
- **Strategic Alignment** - All plans aligned with North Star
- **Measurability** - All progress measurable
- **Completeness** - All dependencies documented
- **Accuracy** - Realistic timelines and estimates
- **Regular Updates** - Keep plans current

### Goal Alignment Validation
**Every hour:**
- Create thought journal entry
- Verify alignment maintained
- Check quality (zero hallucinations?)
- Document progress
- Update active context

---

## 🚨 **CRITICAL RULES**

### Never Skip These
- ❌ **Never work on unaligned tasks** - Must trace to North Star
- ❌ **Never ignore dependencies** - Wait for prerequisites
- ❌ **Never skip priority calculation** - Use formula systematically
- ❌ **Never skip goal alignment check** - Verify hourly
- ❌ **Never skip progress tracking** - Update metrics regularly

### Always Do These
- ✅ **Always trace to North Star** - Every task must connect
- ✅ **Always calculate priority** - Use formula for task selection
- ✅ **Always check confidence** - Only work on ≥0.70 confidence tasks
- ✅ **Always update metrics** - Keep KPIs current
- ✅ **Always validate alignment** - Check hourly

